<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Moving Checklist FAQ</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How far in advance should you start planning a move?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Start about 8 weeks before moving day. That gives you time to compare at least three movers, declutter and give notice on a rental. In the busy May to September season, book movers even earlier. If you have less time, start with the urgent tasks: movers, mail forwarding and utilities.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What should I do 2 weeks before moving?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Two weeks before moving, confirm the date, time and both addresses with the movers or the rental company, plan parking at both homes, refill prescriptions, return borrowed items and take apart furniture you can do without. Keep the screws in a labeled bag taped to each piece.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What is the first thing to do when you move?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Set the moving date and budget, then book movers or a van, because good dates fill up first. Next, give notice if you rent, then declutter before you buy boxes. On arrival, the first jobs are meter readings, making the beds and unpacking the essentials box.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Who do I need to tell when I move?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tell the post office, your bank and card providers, employer, doctor and dentist, insurers, phone and internet provider, subscriptions, school, the tax office and the driving license authority, and update your voter registration. The free PDF has a who-to-tell list you can tick off.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">More Moving Tools</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Work out how many boxes to buy with our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/moving-box-calculator/">moving box calculator</a>, and if your dates do not line up, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/storage-unit-size-calculator/">storage unit size calculator</a> shows what size unit you need. Before you pack, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/closet-clean-out/">closet clean-out</a> guide and tips on <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/how-to-fold-clothes-to-save-space/">how to fold clothes to save space</a> cut the number of boxes, and once you arrive, start with <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/how-to-organize-kitchen-cabinets/">how to organize kitchen cabinets</a>.</p>



